1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,791
Meet Claro, banking support in Spanish and Portuguese.

2
00:00:03,791 --> 00:00:08,073
These screenshots come from actual local test runs with team authored
fixtures.

3
00:00:08,073 --> 00:00:16,698
The application understands transactions, prepares review cases, and completes
a human follow up. It never connects to real bank accounts.

4
00:00:17,598 --> 00:00:20,675
The Portuguese customer asks whether a payment went through.

5
00:00:20,675 --> 00:00:23,424
Claro asks which transaction before answering.

6
00:00:23,424 --> 00:00:31,850
An authorized record tool returns thirty eight dollars and fifty cents as
pending, preserving the currency, source reference, and historical date.

7
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:36,661
This Spanish report describes an unfamiliar charge after a phone call.

8
00:00:36,661 --> 00:00:40,017
The preview preserves that context and redacts the test email.

9
00:00:40,017 --> 00:00:45,354
A separate confirmation is required to create a case. Typing yes in chat
cannot execute it.

10
00:00:45,354 --> 00:00:47,520
No refund or card blocking is promised.

11
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:52,747
Every successful case creation needs a committed record and verified read
back.

12
00:00:52,747 --> 00:00:56,841
Retries keep the same idempotency key and stop after three attempts.

13
00:00:56,841 --> 00:00:59,984
A verification failure never becomes a success claim.

14
00:01:00,884 --> 00:01:04,574
The analyst asks whether the charge was noticed during or after the call.

15
00:01:04,574 --> 00:01:09,033
The Portuguese customer sees that exact question and can answer inside the
case.

16
00:01:09,033 --> 00:01:12,095
A verified reply returns the case to the review queue.

17
00:01:12,995 --> 00:01:18,183
The analyst now sees the original report, the question, and the customer reply
in order.

18
00:01:18,183 --> 00:01:23,291
The review is closed, and all four events remain after refreshing and
switching profiles.

19
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:26,647
The backend stores the history; the browser does not invent it.

20
00:01:27,547 --> 00:01:32,809
One FastAPI service owns sessions, scoped tools, and transactional case
storage.

21
00:01:32,809 --> 00:01:36,912
Jev routing and DeepSeek Flash wording are implemented behind bounded
adapters.

22
00:01:36,912 --> 00:01:43,232
Live inference still requires explicit authorization for metered use. These
captures used local processing.

23
00:01:43,232 --> 00:01:52,008
Provider status and fallback are disclosed. Only entered sandbox messages and
minimized fixture context may leave; organizer data never does.

24
00:01:52,908 --> 00:01:57,138
Language understanding and complete workflow outcomes are evaluated
separately.

25
00:01:57,138 --> 00:02:04,116
The repository preserves offline baselines, failure analysis, language slices,
and service segments.

26
00:02:04,116 --> 00:02:10,017
Authored scenarios and mocked provider tests do not prove real customer
performance or live provider quality.

27
00:02:10,917 --> 00:02:17,895
The fraud candidates did not pass the validation promotion gate. Risk remains
unavailable for these out of domain fixtures.

28
00:02:17,895 --> 00:02:20,573
A low score never dismisses the customer report.

29
00:02:20,573 --> 00:02:29,952
Claro delivers a working bilingual follow up with explicit controls and
measured limits, ready for review, with real banking production still outside
this prototype.
